  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When attempting to upload a new avatar with a minimal setup (it's mine from scratch, so nothing fancy), the SDK starts the upload (which takes like 20-30 minutes, mind you my upload bandwith is 50mbit/s) then fails with the erros in the attached image.\n\nThe file does in fact exist and I do have read/write permissions on it. It's about 20mb big. I'm using unity 2018.4.20f1 with this SDK \"VRCSDK3-AVATAR-2021.07.12.18.52_Public\"\n\nI already cleared all caches and deleted the %APPDATA%/Local/Temp/* files. That did not help.\n\nThe avatar builds and works just fine when testing locally.\n\nReading through that bug report: https://feedback.vrchat.com/sdk-bug-reports/p/upload-fails-with-temp-directory-on-case-sensitive-filesystem-sdk3-world-2021032\n\nI made a junction link to another harddisk and now it's uploading fine. Perhaps this is the same issue that also affects avatars.",
